a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adsense/editor/adsense-delete-dialog.html",'<section class="ga-dialog-title">\n  Are you sure you want to delete this link?\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-content owned-by-user" ng-if="ctrl.currentLinkOwnedByUser">\n  Unlinking this AdSense property from Analytics will stop all data flowing between the AdSense and Analytics properties: <ul> <li>AdSense data (i.e., eCPM, Impressions) won\'t be visible in Analytics reports. AdSense data up until the time you unlink the property will still be available. </li> </ul> \n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-content not-owned-by-user" ng-if="!ctrl.currentLinkOwnedByUser"\n         ng-include="\'/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adsense/editor/permanent-change-msg.html\'">\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-buttons">\n  <ga-button-delete ng-click="$confirm()"></ga-button-delete>\n  <ga-button-cancel ng-click="$cancel()"></ga-button-cancel>\n</section>\n'),
a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adsense/editor/adsense-editor.html",['<header class="title">\n  Configure Adsense Link\n</header>\n<p class="W_FORMS_ITEM_DESCRIPTION">\n  By linking your Analytics property to your AdSense account(s), you will enable data to flow between the products. Data exported from your Analytics property into AdSense is subject to the AdSense terms of service, while AdSense data imported into Analytics is subject to the Analytics terms of service. \n  <a ga-learn-more help-center=adsense answer-id=6084409></a>\n</p>\n<ga-wizard back-sref="app.admin.integrations.adsense.table"\n           on-save="ctrl.save()"\n           read-only="!ctrl.canEdit"\n           initially-completed="!!ctrl.currentLink">\n  <steps>\n    <ga-wizard-step continue-disabled="ctrl.continueDisabled"\n                    on-leave="ctrl.warnIfPermanentChange(cause)">\n      <step-title>\n        Select an AdSense Property\n      </step-title>\n      <step-summary>\n        {{ctrl.getSelectedProperty().publisherCode}}\n        {{ctrl.getSelectedProperty().syndicationProduct}}\n      </step-summary>\n      <step-body>\n\n        <div class="no-account" ng-if="!ctrl.accountToLink">\n          There are no AdSense accounts associated with the Analytics login you\'re using. Make sure that you\'re using a <a answer-id="27439" ga-learn-more="" help-center="accounts"> Google Account </a> (login or email address) that has <a answer-id="2884495" ga-learn-more="">Edit</a> permission for the Analytics property and <a answer-id="2646544" ga-learn-more="" help-center="adsense"> Administrative access </a> for the AdSense account. Alternatively, <a href="https://www.google.com/adsense/start/#sourceid=aso&amp;subid=ww-ww-et-gaaslink" target="_blank"> create a new AdSense account. </a> If you are a premium AdSense user, please contact your AdSense account manager to add or remove links.\n        </div>\n\n        <div class="nothing-to-link" ng-if="ctrl.nothingToLink && ctrl.accountToLink">\n          All of the AdSense properties that you have permission to link are already linked.\n        </div>\n\n        <jfk-zippy class="integrations-zippy" start-collapsed="false"\n                   ng-if="ctrl.accountToLink"\n                   ng-repeat="(publisherCode, account) in ctrl.propertiesByAccount">\n          <div class="goog-zippy-collapsed">\n            <span class="folder"></span>\n            {{publisherCode}}\n          </div>\n          <div class="goog-zippy-content">\n            <div class="ga-form-item">\n              <div ng-repeat="property in account[\'linkable\']">\n                <ga-radiobutton ng-model="ctrl.selectedPropertyCode" value="property.propertyCode"\n                                name="linkedAdsenseProperty" required>\n                  {{property.syndicationProduct}}\n                </ga-radiobutton>\n              </div>\n              <ga-error-label targets="linkedAdsenseProperty"></ga-error-label>\n            </div>\n            <div ng-if="account[\'alreadyLinked\'].length > 0" class="already-linked">\n              <div class="already-linked-summary">\n                <span class="already-linked-indicator"></span>\n                {{ctrl.getAlreadyLinkedSummaryMsg(account)}}\n              </div>\n              <div ng-repeat="link in account[\'alreadyLinked\']" class="already-linked-row">\n                <span class="already-linked-indicator"></span>\n                {{link.syndicationProduct}}\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </jfk-zippy>\n      </step-body>\n    </ga-wizard-step>\n    <ga-wizard-step',
'        confirm-text="'+c("Enable link")+'">','      <step-title>\n        Link configuration\n      </step-title>\n      <step-summary>\n        <div>{{ ctrl.getStepTwoSummaryMsg() }}</div>\n      </step-summary>\n      <step-body>\n        <div class="ga-form-item">\n          <div class="desc">\n            Which Analytics view should this AdSense property link to?\n          </div>\n          <div class="content">\n            <ga-account-tree-picker\n                required\n                name="viewPicker"\n                type="view"\n                single-select="false"\n                ng-model="ctrl.selectedViews"></ga-account-tree-picker>\n          </div>\n          <ga-error-label targets="viewPicker"></ga-error-label>\n        </div>\n      </step-body>\n    </ga-wizard-step>\n  </steps>\n  <extra-global-buttons>\n    <a class="delete-link" ng-if="ctrl.currentLink" ng-click="ctrl.deleteLink()">\n      delete\n    </a>\n  </extra-global-buttons>\n  <whats-next>\n    <a class="delete-link" ng-if="ctrl.currentLink" ng-click="ctrl.deleteLink()">\n      delete\n    </a>\n    <h1>\n      What\'s next?\n    </h1>\n    <p>\n      It may take up to 24 hours for your AdSense link to begin displaying data.\n    </p>\n    <section class="adsense-whtnext">\n      <h2>\n        See AdSense Metrics in Analytics Reports\n      </h2>\n      <p>\n        Add Adsense metrics such as revenue, clicks and impressions to your favorite analytics reports to get a better understanding of how well your pages or content is monetizing. This data can assist in optimizing your site such as the optimal ad load or what type of content to focus on.\n      </p>\n      <a ga-learn-more answer-id=3254288></a>\n    </section>\n  </whats-next>\n</ga-wizard>\n\n'].join("\n")),
a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adsense/editor/adsense-permanent-change-dialog.html",'<section class="ga-dialog-title">\n  Are you sure you want to continue?\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-content"\n         ng-include="\'/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adsense/editor/permanent-change-msg.html\'">\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-buttons">\n  <ga-dialog-buttons-ok-cancel></ga-dialog-buttons-ok-cancel>\n</section>\n'),a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adsense/editor/permanent-change-msg.html",
"<p> <strong>This action is permanent. You will not be able to relink this AdSense property because you do not have permission to access it. </strong> </p> Unlinking this AdSense property from Analytics will stop all data flowing between the AdSense and Analytics properties: <ul> <li>AdSense data (i.e., eCPM, Impressions) won't be visible in Analytics reports. AdSense data up until the time you unlink the property will still be available. </li></ul> \n"),a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adsense/table/adsense-table.html",
'<header class="title">\n  AdSense Linking\n</header>\n\n<ga-table\n    name="adsenseTable"\n    search-enabled="true"\n    sort-enabled="true"\n    sort-function="ctrl.compareRows"\n    default-sort-column-id="adsensePublisherCode"\n    blacklisted-search-keys="[\'view\', \'linkUid\']">\n  <div controls-template>\n    <button type="button" class="ga-table-action-button create-button"\n            ng-disabled="{{!ctrl.canEdit}}" ui-sref="app.admin.integrations.adsense.editor({linkUid: \'new\'})">\n      + New Adsense Link\n    </button>\n  </div>\n  <table>\n    <tr header-template>\n      <th ga-sortable-header-cell sort-key="adsensePublisherCode">\n        AdSense Account\n      </th>\n      <th ga-sortable-header-cell sort-key="syndicationProduct">\n        AdSense Web Property\n      </th>\n      <th ga-sortable-header-cell sort-key="linkedViews">\n        Linked views\n      </th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr row-template>\n      <th>\n        <a ui-sref="app.admin.integrations.adsense.editor({ linkUid: rowData.linkUid })"\n           class="ga-table-edit-link" ng-bind="::rowData.adsensePublisherCode"></a>\n      </th>\n      <td ng-bind="::rowData.syndicationProduct"></td>\n      <td ng-bind="::ctrl.renderNumLinkedViews(rowData)"></td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</ga-table>\n'),
a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adwords/editor/adwords-editor.html",'<h1\n    class="adwords-editor-title"\n    ng-if="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n  Configure Google Ads link\n</h1>\n<h1\n    class="adwords-editor-title"\n    ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n  Configure Google Ads link group\n</h1>\n<div ng-if="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n  <p>\n    By linking your Google Analytics property to your Google Ads account(s), you will enable data to flow between the products. Note that the export of audiences and certain conversion data for personalized additional activation (see below). Data exported from Google Analytics is subject to the terms that govern your use of Google Ads, and data exported from your Google Ads accounts into Google Analytics is subject to the terms that govern your use of Google Analytics. \n    <a ga-learn-more answer-id="1033961" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'1033961\')"></a>\n  </p>\n</div>\n<p ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n  By linking your Analytics property to your Google Ads account(s), you will enable data to flow between the products. Data exported from your Analytics property into Google Ads is subject to the Google Ads terms of service, while Google Ads data imported into Analytics is subject to the Analytics terms of service. \n  <a ga-learn-more answer-id="1033961" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'1033961\')"></a>\n</p>\n\n<ga-wizard back-sref="app.admin.integrations.adwords.table"\n           read-only="::$ctrl.disabled"\n           on-save="$ctrl.onSaveLink()"\n           initially-completed="!$ctrl.isNewLink()">\n  <steps>\n    <ga-wizard-step continue-disabled="$ctrl.selectedAccounts.length == 0"\n                    on-leave="$ctrl.onAccountSelectionStepLeave(cause)">\n      <step-title>\n        Select the Google Ads accounts you want to link\n      </step-title>\n      <step-summary>\n        <ga-adwords-summarized-accounts selected-accounts="$ctrl.selectedAccounts">\n        </ga-adwords-summarized-accounts>\n      </step-summary>\n      <step-body>\n        <div class="google-ads-editor-message-container">\n          <md-icon>error_outline</md-icon>\n          <div class="google-ads-editor-message">\n           To link a GA property to a Google Ads account, you must have \u201cedit\u201d permissions on the GA property and admin access on the Google Ads account. Google Ads accounts for which you have admin access are listed here.\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class="ga-adwords-link-not-ads-user-msg google-ads-editor-message-container"\n             ng-if="::$ctrl.notAdsUser()">\n          <md-icon>error_outline</md-icon>\n          <div class="google-ads-editor-message">\n            <p>\n              There are no Google Ads accounts associated with the Analytics login you\'re using. Make sure that you\'re using a <a answer-id="27439" ga-learn-more="" help-center="accounts" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'accounts_27439\')"> Google Account </a> (login or email address) that has <a answer-id="2884495" ga-learn-more="" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'2884495\')">Edit </a>permission for the Analytics property and <a answer-id="1704346" ga-learn-more="" help-center="adwords" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'adwords_1704346\')"> Administrative access</a> for the Google Ads account.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Don\u2019t have a Google Ads account yet? Now that you are using Google Analytics to understand your audience, <a href="http://ads.google.com/signup?sf=awx_ga&amp;subid=ww-ww-xs-g-ga-prop_set_galinking_1!o2" target="_blank"> use Google Ads to turn them into customers</a>.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class="ga-adwords-link-not-enough-access-msg" ng-if="::$ctrl.notEnoughAccess()">\n          You do not have sufficient permissions in Google Ads to link accounts.\n        </div>\n        <div ng-if="$ctrl.doubleLinkedAccounts.length > 0"\n             class="adwords-linking-editor-double-linked-section">\n          <span class="adwords-linking-tree-warning-indicator"></span>\n          The following serving accounts are linked twice:\n          <ul>\n            <li ng-repeat="account in $ctrl.doubleLinkedAccounts"\n                external-id="{{ ::account.externalCustomerId }}">\n              {{ ::account.descriptiveName }}\n            </li>\n          </ul>\n          This most often is not desired, as it can lead to conflicting linking settings with results that may not be what you want.\n        </div>\n        <div ng-if="::$ctrl.hasLinkableAccounts() && !$ctrl.hasAnythingToLink()"\n             class="adwords-linking-editor-nothing-to-link">\n          All of the Google Ads accounts that you have permission to link are already linked.\n        </div>\n        <div ng-if="$ctrl.hasReachedSelectedWeakLimit()"\n             class="adwords-linking-editor-weak-limit-warning">\n          You are linking a large number of Google Ads accounts. This may impact system performance when fetching data from Google Ads.\n        </div>\n        <div ng-if="$ctrl.hasReachedSelectedScaryLimit()"\n             class="adwords-linking-editor-scary-limit-warning">\n          You are linking a large number of Google Ads accounts. Some reporting data may not be accessible from Google Ads.\n        </div>\n        <div ng-if="$ctrl.isMaxLinkCount()"\n             class="adwords-linking-editor-max-link-count">\n          {{ ::$ctrl.getMaxLinkCountWarning() }}\n        </div>\n        <div ng-if="::$ctrl.hasLinkableAccounts() || $ctrl.selectedAccounts.length > 0">\n          <ga-adwords-tree linkable-accounts="::$ctrl.linkableAccounts"\n                           all-links="::$ctrl.allLinks"\n                           current-link="::$ctrl.currentLink"\n                           is-max-link-count="$ctrl.isMaxLinkCount()"\n                           disabled="::$ctrl.isAccountTreeDisabled()"\n                           name="adwordsTree"\n                           ng-model="$ctrl.selectedAccounts"\n                           ng-change="$ctrl.handleSelectedAccountsChange()"\n                           required>\n          </ga-adwords-tree>\n          <ga-error-label targets="adwordsTree"></ga-error-label>\n        </div>\n      </step-body>\n    </ga-wizard-step>\n    <ga-wizard-step confirm-text="{{ $ctrl.getConfirmButtonText() }}"\n                    on-enter="$ctrl.onLinkConfigurationStepEnter()">\n      <step-title>\n        Link configuration\n      </step-title>\n      <step-summary>\n        <span\n            ng-if="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n          Link title:\n          {{ $ctrl.currentLink.linkName }}\n        </span>\n        <span\n            ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n          Link group title:\n          {{ $ctrl.currentLink.linkName }}<br>\n          {{ $ctrl.getNumViewsUseThisLinkMgs() }}\n        </span>\n      </step-summary>\n      <step-body>\n        <div\n            ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty"\n            class="ga-form-item">\n          <div class="label" ng-attr-id="gaLinkTitleId">\n            Link group title\n          </div>\n          <div class="content">\n            <input type="text"\n                   name="linkName"\n                   ng-disabled="::$ctrl.disabled"\n                   required ng-maxlength="255"\n                   ng-model="$ctrl.currentLink.linkName"\n                   placeholder="e.g., My Company\'s Google Ads Account"\n                   class="galaxy-input medium" />\n            <ga-help-tooltip-ng1 topic-id="4495847"\n                                 role="button"\n                                 ng-attr-aria-labelledby="gaLinkTitleId">\n            </ga-help-tooltip-ng1>\n          </div>\n          <ga-error-label targets="linkName">\n            <ga-error-label-msg catches="required">\n              Enter a link group title.\n            </ga-error-label-msg>\n          </ga-error-label>\n        </div>\n\n        <ga-adwords-view-selector\n            ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty"\n            all-views="::$ctrl.allViews"\n            selected-views="$ctrl.currentLink.view"\n            disabled="::$ctrl.disabled"\n            on-select-views="$ctrl.onSelectViews(selectedViews)">\n        </ga-adwords-view-selector>\n\n        <ga-checkbox\n            ng-if="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty"\n            ng-model="$ctrl.currentLink.scionRemarketingEnabled"\n            name="scionRemarketingEnabled"\n            disabled="::$ctrl.disabled">\n          Enable personalized advertising features with this integration. Automatically publish my Google Analytics audience lists and Google Analytics remarketing events/parameters to the linked Google Ads account. You can change this setting anytime while maintaining your link for other purposes. \n          <a ga-learn-more answer-id="9313634" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'9313634\')"></a>\n        </ga-checkbox>\n\n        <div class="adwords-linking-editor-setting-section adwords-linking-editor-enhanced-conversions-settings-section"\n             ng-if="$ctrl.enhancedConversionsWhitelistEnabled">\n          <div class="text-section">\n            <div class="label">\n                Link my GA property to Google Ads Enhanced Conversions for Processor based web conversion export\n            </div>\n            <div class="content">\n              This setting establishes an additional linking integration between your GA property and Google Ads Enhanced Conversions, which supports the import of web conversions from multiple sources including customer match. By enabling this setting, you will export your analytics web conversions via this new link into Ads Enhanced Conversions, and the data will be subject to the terms that govern the Google Ads Enhanced Conversions feature. All other data (e.g. site statistics, audiences) will continue to flow via your regular linking integration between your GA property and Google Ads account as defined above. To learn more about the features and terms of the EC integration, click here:\n              <a ga-learn-more answer-id="10286444" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'10286444\')"\n                 aria-label="learn more about Enhanced Conversions"\n                 i18n-aria-label="Text for link to learn about Enhanced Conversions"></a>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div class="radio-section">\n            <div class="spacer"></div>\n            <ga-radiobutton ng-model="$ctrl.currentLink.enhancedConversionsEnabled"\n                            value="true"\n                            name="enhancedConversionsEnabled"\n                            disabled="::$ctrl.disabled"\n                            inline="false">\n                  Yes\n            </ga-radiobutton>\n            <ga-radiobutton ng-model="$ctrl.currentLink.enhancedConversionsEnabled"\n                            value="false"\n                            name="enhancedConversionsEnabled"\n                            disabled="::$ctrl.disabled"\n                            inline="false">\n                  No\n            </ga-radiobutton>\n            <div class="spacer"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class="adwords-linking-editor-setting-section adwords-linking-editor-autotagging-settings-section"\n             ng-if="!$ctrl.disabled">\n          <div class="ga-form-item" ng-show="$ctrl.showAdvancedAutoTagging">\n            <div class="label">\n              Advanced Settings\n            </div>\n            <div class="content">\n              <ga-radiobutton ng-model="$ctrl.currentLink.autotaggingForAddedAccountsEnabled"\n                              value="true"\n                              name="enableAutoTagging"\n                              disabled="::$ctrl.disabled"\n                              inline="false">\n                <span ng-if="::$ctrl.isNewLink()">\n                  Enable auto-tagging on all linked Google Ads accounts (recommended)\n                </span>\n                <span ng-if="::!$ctrl.isNewLink()">\n                  <span ng-if="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n                    Enable auto-tagging on any Google Ads accounts that were added to the link (recommended)\n                  </span>\n                  <span ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n                    Enable auto-tagging on any Google Ads accounts that were added to the link group (recommended)\n                  </span>\n                </span>\n              </ga-radiobutton>\n              <div class="adwords-linking-editor-radiobutton-desc">\n                This option appends a unique ID to the end of the destination URL. This ID lets Analytics report the details of each click.\n                <a ga-learn-more answer-id="1733663" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'1733663\')"></a>\n              </div>\n              <br/>\n              <ga-radiobutton ng-model="$ctrl.currentLink.autotaggingForAddedAccountsEnabled"\n                              value="false"\n                              name="enableAutoTagging"\n                              disabled="::$ctrl.disabled"\n                              inline="false">\n                Leave my auto-tagging settings as they are\n              </ga-radiobutton>\n              <div class="adwords-linking-editor-radiobutton-desc">\n                For accounts where auto-tagging is disabled, your data will appear as Google organic traffic until you manually add specific tags.\n                <a ga-learn-more answer-id="1033981" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'1033981\')"></a>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div ng-show="!$ctrl.showAdvancedAutoTagging">\n            <div class="adwords-linking-editor-autotagging-section-icon"></div>\n            <div class="adwords-linking-editor-autotagging-section-content">\n              <div class="adwords-linking-editor-setting-section-title">\n                <span ng-if="::$ctrl.isNewLink()">\n                  Creating this link enables auto-tagging for all linked Google Ads accounts.\n                </span>\n                <span ng-if="::!$ctrl.isNewLink()">\n                  <span ng-if="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n                    Saving this link enables auto-tagging for any Google Ads accounts that were added to the link.\n                  </span>\n                  <span ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n                    Saving this link enables auto-tagging for any Google Ads accounts that were added to the link group.\n                  </span>\n                </span>\n              </div>\n              <div class="adwords-linking-editor-setting-section-desc">\n                Auto-tagging allows Analytics to automatically associate Google Ads data with customer clicks.\n              </div>\n              <a\n                ng-click="::!$ctrl.disabled && $ctrl.switchToAdvancedAutotaggingSettings()"\n                ng-disabled="::$ctrl.disabled"\n                class="adwords-linking-editor-advanced-settings-toggle"\n              >Advanced settings</a>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class="adwords-linking-editor-setting-section"\n             ng-show="$ctrl.showDataSharingSettings">\n          <div class="adwords-linking-editor-setting-section-title">\n            Account Settings: Data Sharing\n          </div>\n          <div class="adwords-linking-editor-setting-section-desc">\n            You need to enable this setting for Analytics data, like Goals and site engagement metrics, to be available in Google Ads.\n          </div>\n          <ga-checkbox ng-model="$ctrl.currentLink.adwordsDataSharingEnabled"\n                       name="adwordsDataSharingEnabled"\n                       disabled="::$ctrl.disabled">\n            Share my Analytics data with linked Google Ads accounts\n          </ga-checkbox>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class="adwords-linking-editor-setting-section adwords-linking-editor-gdn-settings-section"\n             ng-if="$ctrl.isGdnImpressionsEnabled()">\n          <div class="ga-form-item">\n            <div class="label" ga-optional>\n              Additional data\n            </div>\n            <div class="content">\n              <ga-checkbox ng-model="$ctrl.currentLink.gdnImpressionReportingEnabled"\n                           name="gdnImpressionReportingEnabled"\n                           disabled="::$ctrl.disabled">\n                Enable Google Display Network Impression Reporting\n              </ga-checkbox>\n              <div class="adwords-linking-editor-checkbox-desc">\n                You might need to <a answer-id="2444872" ga-learn-more="" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'2444872\')"> enable Advertising Features</a> first. Please note that <a answer-id="2700409" ga-learn-more="" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'2700409\')"> updates to your privacy policy</a> might be required. Please note that this beta does not work for Video ads.\n                <a ga-learn-more answer-id="3105620" ng-click="$ctrl.clickLearnMore(\'3105620\')"></a>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </step-body>\n    </ga-wizard-step>\n  </steps>\n  <extra-global-buttons>\n    <a class="delete-link"\n       ng-if="::!$ctrl.disabled && !$ctrl.isNewLink()"\n       ng-click="$ctrl.deleteLink()">\n      <span\n          ng-if="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n        Delete link\n      </span>\n      <span\n          ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n        Delete link group\n      </span>\n    </a>\n  </extra-global-buttons>\n  <whats-next>\n    <a class="delete-link"\n       ng-if="!$ctrl.disabled && !$ctrl.isNewLink()"\n       ng-click="$ctrl.deleteLink()">\n      <span\n          ng-if="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n        Delete link\n      </span>\n      <span\n          ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n        Delete link group\n      </span>\n    </a>\n    <h2 class="adwords-editor-whats-next-header">\n      What\'s next?\n    </h2>\n    <p>\n      It may take up to 24 hours for your Google Ads link to begin displaying data.\n    </p>\n    <ga-adwords-whats-next-site-engagement\n        ng-if="::!$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty"\n        is-enhanced-property="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n    </ga-adwords-whats-next-site-engagement>\n    <ga-adwords-whats-next-conversions\n        is-enhanced-property="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty"></ga-adwords-whats-next-conversions>\n    <ga-adwords-whats-next-remarketing\n        is-enhanced-property="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty"></ga-adwords-whats-next-remarketing>\n    <ga-adwords-whats-next-display-network\n        ng-if="$ctrl.isGdnImpressionsEnabled() && $ctrl.currentLink.gdnImpressionReportingEnabled"\n        is-enhanced-property="::$ctrl.isEnhancedProperty">\n    </ga-adwords-whats-next-display-network>\n  </whats-next>\n</ga-wizard>\n'),
a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adwords/editor/dialogs/adwords-confirm-no-views-dialog.html",'<section class="ga-dialog-title">\n  Confirm link creation\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-content">\n  <p> You have not selected any views for this Google Ads link. If you want to see Google Ads cost data in Analytics\u2014or Analytics user data or conversions in Google Ads\u2014you must select at least one view. Otherwise, the only data you can share via the link will be remarketing audiences. </p> <p> Do you still want to create a link with no views selected? </p>\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-buttons">\n  <ga-dialog-buttons-ok-cancel></ga-dialog-buttons-ok-cancel>\n</section>\n'),
a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adwords/editor/dialogs/adwords-confirm-permanent-unlink-dialog.html",'<section class="ga-dialog-title">\n  Are you sure you want to unlink these accounts?\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-content">\n  <p>\n    Data from Google Ads (i.e., clicks, impressions, cpc, etc.) will no longer be visible in Analytics reports. Session data up until the time you unlink the account will still be available. Any new sessions that result from clicks in this Google Ads account after you have unlinked will appear in Analytics reports as <a answer-id="2820717" ga-learn-more="">(not set)</a>.\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    Additionally, you do not have Administrative access for some of the Google Ads accounts you\'re attempting to unlink. If you unlink those accounts, you will not be able to re-link them. The following accounts are affected:\n  </p>\n  <div ng-repeat="account in $ctrl.unlinkedAccounts">\n    <div ng-if="::account.mcmAccount"\n         class="adwords-linking-editor-account adwords-linking-editor-mcm-account"\n         external-id="{{ ::account.externalCustomerId }}">\n      <span class="adwords-linking-editor-account-name">\n        {{ ::account.descriptiveName }}\n      </span>\n      <span class="adwords-linking-editor-account-id">\n        {{ ::account.externalCustomerId | adwordsAccountId }}\n      </span>\n    </div>\n    <div ng-if="::!account.mcmAccount"\n         class="adwords-linking-editor-account adwords-linking-editor-serving-account"\n         external-id="{{ ::account.externalCustomerId }}">\n      <span class="adwords-linking-editor-account-id">\n        {{ ::account.externalCustomerId | adwordsAccountId }}\n      </span>\n      <span class="adwords-linking-editor-account-name">\n        {{ ::account.descriptiveName }}\n      </span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-buttons">\n  <ga-dialog-buttons-ok-cancel></ga-dialog-buttons-ok-cancel>\n</section>\n'),
a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adwords/editor/dialogs/adwords-confirm-unlink-dialog.html",'<section class="ga-dialog-title">\n  Are you sure you want to unlink accounts?\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-content">\n  <p>\n    Data from Google Ads (i.e., clicks, impressions, cpc, etc.) will no longer be visible in Analytics reports. Session data up until the time you unlink the account will still be available. Any new sessions that result from clicks in this Google Ads account after you have unlinked will appear in Analytics reports as <a answer-id="2820717" ga-learn-more="">(not set)</a>.\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    The following accounts will be un-linked:\n  </p>\n  <div ng-repeat="account in $ctrl.unlinkedAccounts">\n    <div ng-if="::account.mcmAccount"\n         class="adwords-linking-editor-account adwords-linking-editor-mcm-account"\n         external-id="{{ ::account.externalCustomerId }}">\n      <span class="adwords-linking-editor-account-name">\n        {{ ::account.descriptiveName }}\n      </span>\n      <span class="adwords-linking-editor-account-id">\n        {{ ::account.externalCustomerId | adwordsAccountId }}\n      </span>\n    </div>\n    <div ng-if="::!account.mcmAccount"\n         class="adwords-linking-editor-account adwords-linking-editor-serving-account"\n         external-id="{{ ::account.externalCustomerId }}">\n      <span class="adwords-linking-editor-account-id">\n        {{ ::account.externalCustomerId | adwordsAccountId }}\n      </span>\n      <span class="adwords-linking-editor-account-name">\n        {{ ::account.descriptiveName }}\n      </span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-buttons">\n  <ga-dialog-buttons-ok-cancel></ga-dialog-buttons-ok-cancel>\n</section>\n'),
a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adwords/editor/dialogs/adwords-delete-dialog-enhanced-property.html",'<section class="ga-dialog-title">\n  Are you sure you want to delete this link?\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-content owned-by-user">\n  If you delete this link, all data will stop flowing between the selected Google Ads account and this Analytics property: <ul> <li> Google Ads data (i.e., clicks, impressions, CPC, etc.) won\u2019t be visible in Analytics reports. Session data up until the time you unlink the account will still be available. Any new sessions that result from clicks in these linked Google Ads accounts after you have unlinked will appear in Analytics reports as <a answer-id="2820717" ga-learn-more="">(not set)</a>. </li> <li> Your Analytics Remarketing Audiences will stop accumulating new users in Google Ads. </li> <li> Google Ads will stop importing all conversions. </li> </ul>\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-buttons">\n  <ga-button-delete ng-click="$confirm()"></ga-button-delete>\n  <ga-button-cancel ng-click="$cancel()"></ga-button-cancel>\n</section>\n'),
a.put("/analytics/app/activities/admin/integrations/adwords/editor/dialogs/adwords-delete-dialog.html",'<section class="ga-dialog-title">\n  Are you sure you want to delete this link group?\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-content owned-by-user">\n  If you delete this link group, all data will stop flowing between your Google Ads accounts and Analytics property: <ul> <li> Google Ads data (i.e., clicks, impressions, CPC, etc.) won\u2019t be visible in Analytics reports. Session data up until the time you unlink the account will still be available. Any new sessions that result from clicks in these linked Google Ads accounts after you have unlinked will appear in Analytics reports as <a answer-id="2820717" ga-learn-more="">(not set)</a>. </li> <li> Your Analytics Remarketing Audiences will stop accumulating new users. </li> <li> Google Ads will stop importing all Analytics Goals, Ecommerce transactions, and metrics you configured. </li> </ul>\n</section>\n<section class="ga-dialog-buttons">\n  <ga-button-delete ng-click="$confirm()"></ga-button-delete>\n  <ga-button-cancel ng-click="$cancel()"></ga-button-cancel>\n</section>\n'),
